{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLYHp56rzV8yyoJX6kaAA7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\trelease:\n     2\t  name: hr-helpdesk-agent\n     3\t  version: \"1.8.0\"\n     4\t  git_sha: \"\"            # stamped by CI\n     5\t  agent_type_id: \"\"      # stamped by CI (src/type_id.py, scheme acme-agent-type-id/v1)\n     6\t  image:\n     7\t    repository: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent\n     8\t    digest: \"\"           # stamped by CI\n     9\t    signer: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    10\t    sbom: attached (BuildKit SPDX)\n    11\t    provenance: SLSA v1 via actions/attest-build-provenance\n    12\t  owners:\n    13\t    accountable_party: \"VP People Operations\"\n    14\t    operational_owner: people-platform\n    15\t\n    16\tstakes:\n    17\t  rating: moderate\n    18\t  autonomy: low (every write requires the employee's confirmation)\n    19\t  rationale: >-\n    20\t    Reads one employee's own leave data and the handbook; writes are leave requests that a\n    21\t    manager must still approve in HRIS, and helpdesk tickets. Worst credible harm: disclosure of\n    22\t    one employee's HR data to another employee, or a misleading policy answer.\n    23\t  approved_by: \"Head of Security Engineering, 2026-09-19\"\n    24\t\n    25\tcapability_combination:\n    26\t  untrusted_input: yes (employee messages, handbook passages, tool output)\n    27\t  sensitive_access: yes (leave records, employee-specific HR documents)\n    28\t  external_change_or_send: yes (leave requests, helpdesk tickets)\n    29\t  containment: every consequential tool requires per-action employee approval bound to args\n    30\t\n    31\tharness:\n    32\t  files: [src/]\n    33\t  entrypoints: {agent: \"src.main:app\", gateway: \"src.gateway:app\"}\n    34\tsystem_prompt: {path: prompts/system.md}\n    35\trules_files: []\n    36\tconfiguration: [config/agent.yaml, config/tools.yaml]\n    37\t\n    38\tmodels:\n    39\t  primary:\n    40\t    role: main agent\n    41\t    owner: people-platform\n    42\t    identity: {provider: anthropic, id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, pinning: snapshot, adapter: none}\n    43\t    pinning_source: \"Anthropic models overview, checked 2026-09-15\"\n    44\t    served_version: recorded per call in audit.events.model_served\n    45\t    fine_tune: none\n    46\t    training_runs: not applicable\n    47\t    training_data: provider-undisclosed\n    48\t  helpers: []            # retrieval is Postgres full-text search; no embedding or reranker model\n    49\t\n    50\ttools:\n    51\t  built_in: []\n    52\t  local: [search_policies]\n    53\t  mcp_servers:\n    54\t    - {id: hris, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\", owner: hris-platform, tools: [get_leave_balance, file_leave_request]}\n    55\t    - {id: helpdesk, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\", owner: it-service-desk, tools: [create_ticket]}\n    56\t  policy_version_source: config/tools.yaml#policy_version\n    57\t\n    58\tpermissions:\n    59\t  sts_scopes: [hr.policy.read, hris.leave.read, hris.leave.request, helpdesk.ticket.create]\n    60\t  token_ttl_seconds: 300\n    61\t  database_role: hr_agent (see migrations/001_init.sql grants)\n    62\t\n    63\tmemory: none (conversation state is held per run and discarded; no cross-run memory)\n    64\tretrieval:\n    65\t  store: retrieval.chunks (Postgres FTS)\n    66\t  writers: [hr_docs_ingest]\n    67\t  filters: [quarantined, expires_at, audience/allowed_employees]\n    68\t\n    69\tidentity_bindings:\n    70\t  agent: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent\n    71\t  gateway: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-tool-gateway\n    72\t\n    73\tnetwork: [k8s/networkpolicy.yaml]\n    74\tadmission: [k8s/admission.yaml]\n    75\tbudgets: config/agent.yaml#budgets\n    76\t\n    77\taudit:\n    78\t  store: audit.events, audit.gateway_decisions (Postgres, weekly partitions)\n    79\t  retention: 6 months\n    80\t  readers: hr_audit_reader\n     1\t*                         @acme/people-platform\n     2\t/prompts/                 @acme/people-platform @acme/hr-policy-reviewers\n     3\t/config/                  @acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering\n     4\t/src/gateway.py           @acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering\n     5\t/src/approvals.py         @acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering\n     6\t/k8s/                     @acme/people-platform @acme/platform-security\n     7\t/migrations/              @acme/people-platform @acme/data-platform\n     8\t/release/                 @acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering\n     9\t/.github/                 @acme/platform-security\n    10\t/CODEOWNERS               @acme/platform-security\n     1\t\"\"\"Calls MCP tools through the hr-tool-gateway.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport logging\n     5\timport uuid\n     6\tfrom typing import Any\n     7\t\n     8\timport httpx\n     9\tfrom opentelemetry.propagate import inject\n    10\t\n    11\tfrom .audit import RunContext\n    12\tfrom .credentials import CredentialBroker\n    13\tfrom .tools import ToolSpec\n    14\t\n    15\tlog = logging.getLogger(\"hr_agent.gateway_client\")\n    16\t\n    17\tGATEWAY_URL = \"https://hr-tool-gateway.hr-agent.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\"\n    18\tGATEWAY_AUDIENCE = \"hr-tool-gateway\"\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tclass ToolDenied(Exception):\n    22\t    def __init__(self, reason: str):\n    23\t        super().__init__(reason)\n    24\t        self.reason = reason\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tclass ToolError(Exception):\n    28\t    def __init__(self, status: int, detail: str):\n    29\t        super().__init__(f\"{status}\")\n    30\t        self.status = status\n    31\t        self.detail = detail\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tclass GatewayUnavailable(Exception):\n    35\t    pass\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tclass GatewayClient:\n    39\t    def __init__(self, client: httpx.AsyncClient, creds: CredentialBroker):\n    40\t        self._client = client\n    41\t        self._creds = creds\n    42\t\n    43\t    async def call(\n    44\t        self, spec: ToolSpec, args: dict[str, Any], ctx: RunContext, subject_token: str, *, operation_id: str\n    45\t    ) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    46\t        try:\n    47\t            token = await self._creds.token(\n    48\t                audience=GATEWAY_AUDIENCE, scope=spec.scope, subject_token=subject_token, subject=ctx.subject\n    49\t            )\n    50\t            return await self._post(GATEWAY_URL, token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)\n    51\t        except GatewayUnavailable:\n    52\t            if not spec.direct_route:\n    53\t                raise\n    54\t            log.warning(\"gateway unavailable, using direct route\", extra={\"tool\": spec.qualified})\n    55\t            token = await self._creds.token(\n    56\t                audience=spec.direct_route[\"audience\"], scope=spec.scope,\n    57\t                subject_token=subject_token, subject=ctx.subject,\n    58\t            )\n    59\t            return await self._post(spec.direct_route[\"endpoint\"], token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)\n    60\t\n    61\t    async def _post(\n    62\t        self, url: str, token: str, spec: ToolSpec, args: dict[str, Any], ctx: RunContext, operation_id: str\n    63\t    ) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    64\t        tool_name = spec.qualified.split(\"/\", 1)[1]\n    65\t        headers = {\n    66\t            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n    67\t            \"Mcp-Method\": \"tools/call\",\n    68\t            \"Mcp-Name\": tool_name,\n    69\t            \"Idempotency-Key\": operation_id,\n    70\t            \"X-Agent-Instance\": ctx.agent_instance_id,\n    71\t            \"X-Agent-Type-Id\": ctx.agent_type_id,\n    72\t        }\n    73\t        inject(headers)\n    74\t        body = {\n    75\t            \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n    76\t            \"id\": str(uuid.uuid4()),\n    77\t            \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n    78\t            \"params\": {\"name\": tool_name, \"arguments\": args, \"_meta\": {\"server\": spec.server}},\n    79\t        }\n    80\t        try:\n    81\t            resp = await self._client.post(url, json=body, headers=headers, timeout=10.0)\n    82\t        except (httpx.ConnectError, httpx.ConnectTimeout) as exc:\n    83\t            raise GatewayUnavailable(str(exc)) from exc\n    84\t        except httpx.TimeoutException as exc:\n    85\t            raise ToolError(504, f\"no response; outcome unknown for operation {operation_id}\") from exc\n    86\t        if resp.status_code == 503:\n    87\t            raise GatewayUnavailable(resp.text[:200])\n    88\t        if resp.status_code in (401, 403, 429):\n    89\t            raise ToolDenied(resp.json().get(\"error\", \"denied\"))\n    90\t        if resp.status_code >= 400:\n    91\t            raise ToolError(resp.status_code, resp.json().get(\"detail\", resp.text))\n    92\t        payload = resp.json()\n    93\t        if \"error\" in payload:\n    94\t            raise ToolError(200, str(payload[\"error\"].get(\"message\", \"\")))\n    95\t        return payload[\"result\"][\"structuredContent\"]\n     1\tapiVersion: v1\n     2\tkind: Namespace\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: hr-agent\n     5\t  labels:\n     6\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n     7\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.31\n     8\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n     9\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n    10\t    istio.io/dataplane-mode: ambient\n    11\t---\n    12\tapiVersion: kyverno.io/v1\n    13\tkind: ClusterPolicy\n    14\tmetadata:\n    15\t  name: hr-agent-verify-images\n    16\t  annotations:\n    17\t    policies.kyverno.io/owner: people-platform\n    18\tspec:\n    19\t  validationFailureAction: Enforce\n    20\t  failurePolicy: Fail\n    21\t  webhookTimeoutSeconds: 15\n    22\t  background: false\n    23\t  rules:\n    24\t    - name: only-approved-registry\n    25\t      match:\n    26\t        any:\n    27\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    28\t      validate:\n    29\t        message: \"Images in hr-agent must come from registry.acme.example and be referenced by digest.\"\n    30\t        pattern:\n    31\t          spec:\n    32\t            =(initContainers):\n    33\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    34\t            containers:\n    35\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    36\t    - name: verify-signature-and-provenance\n    37\t      match:\n    38\t        any:\n    39\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    40\t      verifyImages:\n    41\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent*\"]\n    42\t          mutateDigest: false\n    43\t          verifyDigest: true\n    44\t          required: true\n    45\t          attestors:\n    46\t            - entries:\n    47\t                - keyless:\n    48\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    49\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    50\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n    51\t          attestations:\n    52\t            - type: https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\n    53\t              attestors:\n    54\t                - entries:\n    55\t                    - keyless:\n    56\t                        subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    57\t                        issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    58\t              conditions:\n    59\t                - all:\n    60\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.buildType }}\"\n    61\t                      operator: Equals\n    62\t                      value: \"https://actions.github.io/buildtypes/workflow/v1\"\n    63\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.repository }}\"\n    64\t                      operator: Equals\n    65\t                      value: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent\"\n    66\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.ref }}\"\n    67\t                      operator: Equals\n    68\t                      value: \"refs/heads/main\"\n    69\t                    - key: \"{{ runDetails.builder.id }}\"\n    70\t                      operator: Equals\n    71\t                      value: \"https://github.com/actions/runner/github-hosted\"\n    72\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/platform/*\"]\n    73\t          mutateDigest: false\n    74\t          verifyDigest: true\n    75\t          required: true\n    76\t          attestors:\n    77\t            - entries:\n    78\t                - keyless:\n    79\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/platform-images/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    80\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    81\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n67:                log.error(\"lookalike tool name across servers\", extra={\"tool\": name})\n74:                log.error(\"tool fingerprint mismatch; disabled\", extra={\"tool\": spec.qualified})\n134:        \"\"\"INSERT INTO audit.gateway_decisions (ts, traceparent, tenant, accountable_party, operational_owner,\n137:        request.headers.get(\"traceparent\") or \"missing\", owner[\"tenant\"], owner[\"accountable_party\"],\n179:                   \"traceparent\": request.headers.get(\"traceparent\", \"\")}\n193:        log.exception(\"gateway check failed\", extra={\"tool\": tool})\n211:                log.exception(\"fingerprint refresh failed; disabling MCP tools\")\n     1\tname: release\n     2\t\n     3\ton:\n     4\t  push:\n     5\t    branches: [main]\n     6\t\n     7\tpermissions:\n     8\t  contents: read\n     9\t\n    10\tjobs:\n    11\t  build:\n    12\t    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    13\t    environment: production   # requires approval from @acme/people-platform-release\n    14\t    permissions:\n    15\t      contents: read\n    16\t      packages: write\n    17\t      id-token: write\n    18\t      attestations: write\n    19\t    env:\n    20\t      PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE: \"1\"\n    21\t      IMAGE: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent\n    22\t    steps:\n    23\t      - uses: actions/checkout@11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683 # v4.2.2\n    24\t      - uses: actions/setup-python@0b93645e9fea7318ecaed2b359559ac225c90a2b # v5.3.0\n    25\t        with: {python-version: \"3.12.7\"}\n    26\t      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n    27\t        with: {cosign-release: \"v2.6.2\"}\n    28\t      - run: pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n    29\t      - run: python -m pytest -q tests/release\n    30\t      - name: Build and push\n    31\t        id: build\n    32\t        uses: docker/build-push-action@263435318d21b8e681c14492fe198d362a7d2c83 # v6.18.0\n    33\t        with:\n    34\t          push: true\n    35\t          tags: ${{ env.IMAGE }}:${{ github.sha }}\n    36\t          sbom: true\n    37\t          provenance: mode=max\n    38\t      - name: Sign image\n    39\t        run: cosign sign --yes \"${IMAGE}@${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\"\n    40\t      - uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@e8998f949152b193b063cb0ec769d69d929409be # v2.4.0\n    41\t        with:\n    42\t          subject-name: ${{ env.IMAGE }}\n    43\t          subject-digest: ${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\n    44\t          push-to-registry: true\n    45\t      - name: Compute agent-type-id\n    46\t        id: typeid\n    47\t        run: |\n    48\t          python -m src.type_id \"${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\" > type-id.json\n    49\t          echo \"id=$(jq -r .agent_type_id type-id.json)\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n    50\t      - name: Stamp release manifest\n    51\t        run: |\n    52\t          yq -i '.release.agent_type_id = \"${{ steps.typeid.outputs.id }}\" |\n    53\t                 .release.image.digest = \"${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\" |\n    54\t                 .release.git_sha = \"${{ github.sha }}\"' release/manifest.yaml\n    55\t      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4.6.2\n    56\t        with:\n    57\t          name: release-${{ github.sha }}\n    58\t          path: [type-id.json, release/manifest.yaml]\n    59\t\n    60\t  deploy:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ed5773-a566-47b2-9286-6c65525da62e","uuid":"ecbfbff4-d188-40cd-8106-d17eada042d0","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:56:51.468Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\trelease:\n     2\t  name: hr-helpdesk-agent\n     3\t  version: \"1.8.0\"\n     4\t  git_sha: \"\"            # stamped by CI\n     5\t  agent_type_id: \"\"      # stamped by CI (src/type_id.py, scheme acme-agent-type-id/v1)\n     6\t  image:\n     7\t    repository: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent\n     8\t    digest: \"\"           # stamped by CI\n     9\t    signer: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    10\t    sbom: attached (BuildKit SPDX)\n    11\t    provenance: SLSA v1 via actions/attest-build-provenance\n    12\t  owners:\n    13\t    accountable_party: \"VP People Operations\"\n    14\t    operational_owner: people-platform\n    15\t\n    16\tstakes:\n    17\t  rating: moderate\n    18\t  autonomy: low (every write requires the employee's confirmation)\n    19\t  rationale: >-\n    20\t    Reads one employee's own leave data and the handbook; writes are leave requests that a\n    21\t    manager must still approve in HRIS, and helpdesk tickets. Worst credible harm: disclosure of\n    22\t    one employee's HR data to another employee, or a misleading policy answer.\n    23\t  approved_by: \"Head of Security Engineering, 2026-09-19\"\n    24\t\n    25\tcapability_combination:\n    26\t  untrusted_input: yes (employee messages, handbook passages, tool output)\n    27\t  sensitive_access: yes (leave records, employee-specific HR documents)\n    28\t  external_change_or_send: yes (leave requests, helpdesk tickets)\n    29\t  containment: every consequential tool requires per-action employee approval bound to args\n    30\t\n    31\tharness:\n    32\t  files: [src/]\n    33\t  entrypoints: {agent: \"src.main:app\", gateway: \"src.gateway:app\"}\n    34\tsystem_prompt: {path: prompts/system.md}\n    35\trules_files: []\n    36\tconfiguration: [config/agent.yaml, config/tools.yaml]\n    37\t\n    38\tmodels:\n    39\t  primary:\n    40\t    role: main agent\n    41\t    owner: people-platform\n    42\t    identity: {provider: anthropic, id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, pinning: snapshot, adapter: none}\n    43\t    pinning_source: \"Anthropic models overview, checked 2026-09-15\"\n    44\t    served_version: recorded per call in audit.events.model_served\n    45\t    fine_tune: none\n    46\t    training_runs: not applicable\n    47\t    training_data: provider-undisclosed\n    48\t  helpers: []            # retrieval is Postgres full-text search; no embedding or reranker model\n    49\t\n    50\ttools:\n    51\t  built_in: []\n    52\t  local: [search_policies]\n    53\t  mcp_servers:\n    54\t    - {id: hris, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\", owner: hris-platform, tools: [get_leave_balance, file_leave_request]}\n    55\t    - {id: helpdesk, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\", owner: it-service-desk, tools: [create_ticket]}